{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>You shall prepare the road.</b> The road should be wide, trodden, and straight, so that he not lose his way going to the city of refuge. Rabbi Avin says in the name of Rabbi Yaakov: at every fork they would put up a signpost, and at every signpost there would be a marker, and the marker's hand would be turned, pointing in the direction of the city of refuge. And that is the meaning of 'על כן יורה חטאים בדרך' (therefore he instructs the sinners on the way)." "<b>And you shall divide the border of your land.</b> How so? The land of Israel was four hundred parasangs: from the south to Chevron, one hundred parasangs; from Chevron to Shekhem, one hundred parasangs; from Shekhem to Kadesh, one hundred parasangs; from Kadesh to the north, one hundred parasangs. It turns out that the cities of refuge at the two ends, to the north and to the south, are far from the middle ones by a great deal. And that is the Talmudic discussion: what is the difference between the ones on this side, which are far, and the one in the middle, which is close? And they answer: in Shekhem too murderers are common, as it is written, 'חבר כהנים דרך ירצחו שכמה' (a company of priests by murder travel together)." "<b>Any murderer.</b> Whether intentional or unintentional, as was explained above in the portion of Masei."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:53:26.175363347Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}